nt story we have seen a massive  deregulation regarding environmental  loss and that of course benefits a kind  of predatory Agro business  producers who don't really care about  the environment and who have pushed a  very strong agenda and that of course  has an impact on the indigenous  populations as well because we have many  indigenous peoples living in protected  areas in Brazil  Vietnam  [Music]  deforestation rates in Brazil spiked  during bolsonaro's presidency  his refusal to enforce the law has  helped push parts of the Amazon closer  to what some scientists fear could be a  Tipping Point where the rainforest turns  into dry grassland  bolsonaro's presidency has brought  religion into politics too  nearly a third of Brazilians identifies  Evangelical  at the last election 70 of them voted  for bolsonaro  Evangelical pastors present him as a  protector of family values and leave  their congregations in no doubt what's  at stake should his opponents take power  foreign  the way bolsonaro has dealt with  Evangelical uh voters by by saying that  he's the only president in Brazil in the  history of Brazil who will be using God  he's the only president who really loves  evangelicals even though he himself is a  Catholic and by trying to bridge this  Catholic Protestant dividing the country  by presenting himself as a pen Christian  president bolsonaru is able to capture  the the the love and the support and the  Loyalty of these holders  foreign  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  has persuaded his supporters of another  higher truth that he represents the  authentic will of the people when courts  rule against him bolsonaro suggests  they're biased when the media criticize  him he dismisses them as Peddlers of  fake news  [Music]  many of his supporters now believe that  any institution that stands in his way  is wicked and must be challenged also  now keeps spitting his supporters  against political institutions because  well that's what populists generally do  th